      ],
      "description": "A ==Home Assistant integration that controls Samsung SmartThings appliances over the home network== instead of Samsung's cloud. It talks to washers, dryers, fridges, air conditioners, ovens and more using the OCF standard over CoAP and DTLS, and is installable from HACS's default list.",
      "why_interesting": "Local control is what many smart-home owners want and few vendors offer. The README says that ==after setup it never contacts Samsung's servers==, and it maps each appliance type through declarative tables tested against 90+ real captures. Version 0.37.0, released this morning, adds a soundbar media player and a first robot vacuum.",
      "caveat": "This is a personal community project, not a Samsung product. Setup contacts Samsung once, ==some appliances refuse its automatic certificate== and need a pre-shared key it cannot obtain, appliances must stay registered in SmartThings, and the robot vacuum's write controls are not yet confirmed on hardware."
    },
