      ],
      "description": "A ==context-compression layer for coding agents== that folds consumed conversation into layered summaries, so one session can keep running for days inside a small context window. It installs a bili command that works as a native plugin for some agents and as a local proxy for others.",
      "why_interesting": "Long agent sessions hit context limits and token bills. This project ==supports a long list of agent clients== and publishes a preprint and benchmark write-ups in its repository; the maintainer claims about 5 times fewer tokens and a 100K window being enough, which we have not verified.",
      "caveat": "For clients without a plugin seam it runs as a ==TLS-intercepting proxy with its own certificate==, which sees all model traffic. The benchmarks are hosted in its own repository, and the licence adds a visible-attribution requirement on top of MIT."
    },
